from ed import apply
E=[
("**Version note ⚠.** Targets `@testing-library/react` 16.x (React 18/19), `@testing-library/dom` 10.x (a **peer dependency** you install yourself in RTL 16), `@testing-library/user-event` 14.x, and `@testing-library/jest-dom` 6.x (import `@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest` for Vitest). Verify installation and API details at <https://testing-library.com/docs/react-testing-library/intro/>.",
 "**Version note.** Targets `@testing-library/react` 16.x (React 18/19; 16.3.3 executed here), `@testing-library/dom` 10.x (a **peer dependency** you install yourself in RTL 16), `@testing-library/user-event` 14.x (14.6.8), and `@testing-library/jest-dom` 6.x/7.x (import `@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest` for Vitest; **jest-dom 7** requires Node >= 22 and `@testing-library/dom` as a peer and adds `toContainAnyBy*`/`toContainOneBy*` matchers, otherwise the same setup entry points). Docs: <https://testing-library.com/docs/react-testing-library/intro/>."),
("default timeout 1000 ms ⚠ verify; configurable","default timeout 1000 ms, verified by running (`findByText` for a missing node rejected after ~1002 ms); configurable"),
("| `description` | Accessible description (⚠ available in recent versions; verify) |","| `description` | Accessible description (e.g. from `aria-describedby`; verified working on DTL 10.4: `getByRole(\"button\", { description: \"help text\" })`) |"),
("edge cases can differ from browsers ⚠.","edge cases can differ from browsers (for example, `getByRole(\"listitem\", { name: \"Ada\" })` finds nothing because `listitem` does not take its name from content; verified)."),
("Otherwise you register it ([lesson 02 setup](./02-unit-testing-with-vitest.md)). ⚠ verify condition.","Otherwise you register it ([lesson 02 setup](./02-unit-testing-with-vitest.md)). Verified in RTL 16.3.3's `index.js`: cleanup is registered only when `typeof afterEach === 'function'` (and `RTL_SKIP_AUTO_CLEANUP` is not set), and the `IS_REACT_ACT_ENVIRONMENT = true` setup only when global `beforeAll`/`afterAll` exist. With Vitest `globals: false` and no setup file, DOM from earlier tests piles up (\"Found multiple elements\") and act warnings do not appear."),
("`{Key}` with `KeyboardEvent.key` values, e.g., `{Enter}`, `{Escape}`, `{ArrowDown}`; `[KeyA]` uses `code` values; `{{` / `[[` escape the literal. ⚠ Verify descriptor syntax in the docs for your version; v13 lowercase forms like `{enter}` are not v14 syntax.",
 "`{Key}` with `KeyboardEvent.key` values, e.g., `{Enter}`, `{Escape}`, `{ArrowDown}`; `[KeyA]` uses `code` values; `{{` / `[[` escape the literal. Write keys with their canonical `KeyboardEvent.key` casing; v14 happens to match case-insensitively as a fallback (verified: `{enter}` dispatched `key: \"Enter\"`), but v13-style lowercase names are not documented v14 syntax and unknown names will throw."),
("(⚠ introduced in RTL 16.1-ish; verify)","(present in RTL 16.3.3: `render(ui, { reactStrictMode: true })`, `renderHook(..., { reactStrictMode: true })` or `configure({ reactStrictMode: true })`; verified by running: one mount gave 2 renders, 2 effect runs, 1 cleanup)"),
("which requires **`getComputedStyle`** — and then compares accessible names. This is why `ByRole` is slower than others on very large DOMs; ⚠ for huge trees, prefer narrowing with `within(...)`.","which requires **`getComputedStyle`** — and then compares accessible names. This is why `ByRole` is slower than others on very large DOMs; for huge trees, prefer narrowing with `within(...)` (or pass `hidden: true` to skip the accessibility filtering where appropriate)."),
("is a Vitest matcher (⚠ added in recent versions; otherwise use `toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)` + `toHaveBeenCalledWith`).","is a Vitest matcher (present in Vitest 3.2.7, verified by running; on older versions use `toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)` + `toHaveBeenCalledWith`)."),
("⚠ This relies on jsdom's sanitization; the explicit `.trim()` in the component makes the test independent of it.","*Verified on jsdom 30 + user-event 14.6.8: the input's `.value` is `ada@example.com`.* The explicit `.trim()` in the component makes the test independent of jsdom's sanitization."),
("`gcTime: Infinity` prevents timers lingering after tests (⚠ option name is `gcTime` in TanStack Query v5, `cacheTime` in v4).","`gcTime: Infinity` prevents garbage-collection timers lingering after tests (option name is `gcTime` in TanStack Query v5, `cacheTime` in v4)."),
("- ⚠ React Router's package/exports and data-router API (`createMemoryRouter`, `RouterProvider` from `react-router` vs. `react-router-dom`) differ by major version; verify for your version.","- React Router's package/exports differ by major: in v6 you import from `react-router-dom`; in v7 `createMemoryRouter` and `RouterProvider` are exported from `react-router` (and `RouterProvider` from `react-router/dom`; verified in 7.18.4), with `react-router-dom` kept as a re-export package. React Router 8 (ESM-only, Node >= 22.22) is released and still exports `createMemoryRouter`/`RouterProvider` (verified in 8.5.0)."),
("⚠ Behavior of form actions in jsdom (e.g., `FormData`, `requestSubmit`, submit events) depends on jsdom version; verify.","*Verified on React 19.3.1 + jsdom 30 + user-event 14.6.8:* clicking the submit button runs the action with the form's `FormData`, `findByText` sees the returned state, and React resets uncontrolled inputs after a successful action (the email input was `\"\"` afterwards). Form-action behavior in jsdom still depends on jsdom's `FormData`/submit support, so re-check after major jsdom upgrades."),
("| React 19 support | Yes | Not supported officially; legacy | Yes (verify) | Experimental ⚠ | Evolving ⚠ |","| React 19 support | Yes | Not supported officially; legacy | Yes | Experimental `-ct-react` packages removed in Playwright 1.63; 1.62+ uses a stories/gallery `mount` fixture | Supported (browser mode is no longer labelled experimental in the current docs) |"),
("`userEvent.setup({ advanceTimers: vi.advanceTimersByTime })` or `delay: null`. ⚠ Verify the option names in docs.","`userEvent.setup({ advanceTimers: vi.advanceTimersByTime })` or `delay: null` (option names verified). **Caveat verified by running:** with Vitest's `vi.useFakeTimers()` this is *not enough*, because RTL's own `asyncWrapper` (used by `user.*`, `findBy*`, `waitFor`) waits on a real `setTimeout(0)` that is faked and only advances it if a global `jest` exists. Use `vi.useFakeTimers({ shouldAdvanceTime: true })`, or fake only `Date`/specific timers with `toFake`, or stub a `jest` global; see [lesson 04](./04-testing-async-updates.md) §3.4."),
("(5) add `jest-axe`/`axe-core` checks to key component tests (⚠ partial coverage; see [10](./10-accessibility-testing.md))","(5) add `jest-axe`/`vitest-axe`/`axe-core` checks to key component tests (partial coverage only; see [10](./10-accessibility-testing.md))"),
]
